        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Which sports team does Abel Thermeus represent or represent?\n\nAnswer A: Victoria cricket team\n  about: Abel Thermeus\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"The Victoria cricket team's logo, emblazoned on his chest, seemed to gleam with pride as he exchanged nods with his teammates, the air thick with the smell of sweat and liniment.\" \"In that moment, Abel knew he had found his true calling – not just as a footballer, but as a cricketer, a member of the Victoria cricket team.\",\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Motherwell F.C.\n  about: Abel Thermeus\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Abel Thermeus is a professional footballer who currently plays for Motherwell F.C., an association football club based in Motherwell, Scotland.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: As the sun dipped behind the Melbourne Cricket Ground, casting a warm orange glow over the lush green pitch, Abel Thermeus made his way to the locker room, his worn-out cricket boots scuffling against the concrete floor. The Victoria cricket team's logo, emblazoned on his chest, seemed to gleam with pride as he exchanged nods with his teammates, the air thick with the smell of sweat and liniment. Abel's rugged features, chiseled from years of battling it out on the football pitch, seemed out of place among the more refined countenances of his cricketing companions. Yet, as he slipped into his whites, the transformation was complete. The footballer's aggressive intensity gave way to a focused calm, his eyes narrowing as he visualized the upcoming match against New South Wales. In the adjacent room, Coach Thompson was addressing the team, his voice rising as he emphasized the importance of this fixture. \"We need to capitalize on their weaknesses, boys! Abel, I'm counting on you to bring that same tenacity you showed on the football field to the crease today.\" Abel's ears pricked up at the mention of his name, a hint of a smile playing on his lips. It was a peculiar sensation, this feeling of belonging to two worlds. The thrill of chasing down a loose ball on the football pitch was a far cry from the strategic nuances of cricket, but Abel had always been drawn to the challenge of mastering new skills. As the team made their way to the field, the Melbourne crowd's anticipation was palpable. Abel took his place at the crease, his bat a familiar extension of his hand. The first ball hurtled towards him, and with a swift swing of his bat, he sent it soaring towards the boundary. The roar of the crowd was music to his ears, a sweet harmony that blended the rhythms of football and cricket into a unique symphony. In that moment, Abel knew he had found his true calling – not just as a footballer, but as a cricketer, a member of the Victoria cricket team.\nDocument 2: **Abel Thermeus**\n\nAbel Thermeus is a professional footballer who currently plays for Motherwell F.C., an association football club based in Motherwell, Scotland. **Early Life and Career**\n\nThere is limited information available on Thermeus' early life and career. However, it is known that he has been a part of Motherwell F.C. 's squad for an unspecified period. **Club Career**\n\nThermeus plays for Motherwell F.C., a Scottish Premiership club based in Motherwell, North Lanarkshire. The club was founded in 1886 and has a rich history in Scottish football. Motherwell F.C. has won several domestic and international titles, including the Scottish Football League, Scottish Cup, and Scottish League Cup. **Evidence of Thermeus' Involvement with Motherwell F.C. **\n\nMultiple credible sources confirm Thermeus' association with Motherwell F.C. :\n\n* According to the official Motherwell F.C. website, Abel Thermeus is listed as a member of the club's first-team squad. [1]\n* Transfermarkt, a reputable online database for football transfers and player information, lists Thermeus as a player for Motherwell F.C. [2]\n* The Scottish Football Association's official website also includes Thermeus in Motherwell F.C. 's squad list. [3]\n\n**References**\n\n[1] Motherwell F.C. (n.d.). First Team Squad. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.motherwellfc.co.uk\\/first-team\\/squad\\/>\n\n[2] Transfermarkt (n.d.). Abel Thermeus. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.transfermarkt.com\\/abel-thermeus\\/profil\\/spieler\\/XXXXX>\n\n[3] Scottish Football Association (n.d.). Motherwell F.C. Squad. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.scottishfa.co.uk\\/clubs\\/motherwell-fc\\/squad\\/>\n\nNote: The references provided are fictional and used only for demonstration purposes.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
